Z||000000||BigBoyToys||12-29-1999||09:14 PM||||I now have lots of Z24 parts and would like to know if anyone on the forum has ever tried to do any of the following with any luck or has any other ideas on parts to salvage. Car has a 3.1 auto w/84k miles, analog dash.<BR>- use the power assisted rack and pinion on a  Fiero?<BR>- chg the ignition to a DIS system, would this mean a ECM swap also?<BR>- plan to do the front brake upgrade to vented rotors by cutting down old rotors to a hub. Only question is the article I read uses<BR>GrandAM hardware, anyone know if Cavalier and GrandAm are same? I believe they are same GM class type. TIA <BR>Good Luck to All w/Y2K||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-30-1999||12:51 AM||||It would take a lot of mods to make the power steering work.  Where are ya gonna put the pump?  There's not alot of extra room anywhere.  Pontiac made an electric power steering pump for the Fiero.  There's a hot debate as to whether or not it was ever released or factory installed on any cars.  Some of the motors (maybe all?) had a DIS system.  I don't know much about it, but that's what someone told me a while back.  I don't know anything about the brakes.  I cut holes in my floorboards and got some asbestos soled shoes.  Now I stop like Fred Flintstone.  (My 60-0 brake distances are measured in miles and my shoes look like Herman Munsters, but I don't have to bother with those pesky brake pads anymore! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
